{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish an offline-rhel8 repository from node1 over HTTP on TCP 8080 containing zsh, its dependency closure, repository metadata, and public signing keys.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 staged 161 RPMs including zsh, generated metadata, published the repository and keys, and node2 directly received HTTP 200 responses and loaded all 161 packages through offline-rhel8 on port 8080.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8551e3321aff4624","cmd-25d3bf77e4e54858","cmd-407c6c76a0ac40cf","cmd-34149029afc64cd0","cmd-3cb2b4352e1b494e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sign repository metadata and enforce repository-metadata and RPM signature verification on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The metadata detached signature verifies against the published offline-repository key, all 161 RPMs passed signature checks, and node2's effective configuration has repo_gpgcheck=1 and gpgcheck=1 with both required public keys. The signed zsh package was successfully installed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-25d3bf77e4e54858","cmd-07821e43c6924e4c","cmd-73d9a01849b94e04","cmd-97a9ef3d658c4a55"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Set offline-rhel8 to priority 10 and give every other enabled repository priority 90 or lower preference.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective enabled-repository listing contains offline-rhel8 plus the two Red Hat repositories; offline-rhel8 is priority 10 and both other enabled repositories are priority 90, including after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-73d9a01849b94e04","cmd-72f8b15c9f3642c2"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Install a functional zsh package on node2 from offline-rhel8.","status":"satisfied","summary":"DNF installed zsh-5.5.1-10.el8 explicitly from offline-rhel8, RPM reported its Red Hat RSA/SHA-256 signature, repoquery recorded offline-rhel8 as its source, and the binary ran successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-97a9ef3d658c4a55","cmd-73d9a01849b94e04"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep zsh reinstallable from offline-rh